{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 1, "cost_per_unit": "About 4.1 s of profiled time over 66k tokens, so roughly 60 \u00b5s per token under the profiler. Lexing is about 13 \u00b5s per token: sequential regex tries plus a deque/islice consume call. The rest is grouping-pass scanning, plus building each new TokenList value by re-flattening its whole subtree.", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Doubling the statement count roughly doubles the time, because the work is linear in tokens. Doubling the size of a single statement grows the group-value computation as O(n times nesting depth). That is mildly superlinear, while lexing and scanning stay linear.", "gap": "Each statement text is lexed twice with identical results, once for format and once for parse. Every group_tokens call re-flattens the whole subtree to compute the value, and nested groups do this repeatedly. Each lexed token also pays for creating an islice and a deque.", "least_work": "Lex each distinct statement text once, which is one match per token. Group once per call with a constant number of passes. Build each group's text from its children's already-known text, which is O(children) and not O(subtree leaves).", "library": "sqlparse", "run": 2, "unit_count": "About 66k lexed tokens. Grouping makes 751k Token.match calls, 524k imt calls, 499k ttype __contains__ calls, 743k flatten generator frames and 105k _token_matching scans. That is roughly 10 to 12 match or imt calls per lexed token.", "unit_of_work": "A lexed token. The profile shows 66,078 get_tokens generator resumes across three lexing passes: split on the whole script, then format and parse on each statement. That is about 22k tokens per pass. Each statement's tokens are then grouped twice (format and parse), and each grouping runs about 26 p"}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 6, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "recombine", "