{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 13, "cost_per_unit": "Under the profiler, roughly 6.5 us of get_tokens self time per lexed token, coming from the sequential regex tries, the enumerate loop and a consume(deque(islice)) call per token. Each imt or match call costs about 0.4-0.5 us. Each flatten resumption costs about 0.2 us, and a leaf at depth d pays d ", "deal_round": 2, "doubling": "Doubling the number of statements roughly doubles wall time, since all work is per statement. Doubling the size or nesting of a single statement grows time somewhat faster than linearly, because group construction and flatten re-walk subtrees at O(depth) cost per leaf.", "gap": "The script is lexed three times and grouped twice. About 26 recursive passes each copy the token list and call generic matchers through lambda -> imt -> match chains. Every group creation and every flatten walks the subtree through nested generators at O(depth) per leaf. The lexer pays an extra Pyth", "least_work": "Lex each character once. Build one token tree per statement in a constant number of linear passes. Produce each output string from a single traversal of leaves at O(1) cost per leaf.", "library": "sqlparse", "run": 2, "unit_count": "About 66k token yields from get_tokens, because each statement is lexed three times (split, format, parse). Grouping runs twice per statement (format and parse): 71,992 _group calls, 9,820 _group_matching calls, 105k _token_matching scans, 751k Token.match calls, 524k imt calls, 499k _TokenType.__co", "unit_of_work": "One lexed token carried through the pipeline: matched in Lexer.get_tokens, wrapped as sql.Token in StatementSplitter.process, then visited by about 26 grouping passes (_group, _group_matching, @recurse walks using token_next_by -> imt -> match / ttype __contains__), then flattened again for value st"}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 2, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "recombine", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "leap", "served_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "resolve_tradeoff", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "eliminate", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "far", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}, {"lane": "name_the_problem", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "2e3ad30b"}], "procedures": [{"cell": 13, "deal_round": 2, "failure": null, "framework": "bentley", "functions": "sqlparse/lexer.py::Lexer.get_tokens", "hypothesis_id": null, "idea_id": "leap-01", "library": "sqlparse", "not_applicable": null, "outcome": "idea", "position": 1, "reason": null, "run": 2, "seed": "portfolio-leap-2026-11", "steps_present": "1,2,3,4,5", "steps_required": 5, "title": "Lexer.get_tokens: integer cursor jumping to m.end() instead of enumerate + consu...", "tool": null}, {"cell": 13, "deal_round": 2, "failure": null, "framework": "recall", "functions": "sqlparse/sql.py::TokenList.flatten", "hypothesis_id": "73162a17-d6fc-4105-bd77-98ee33df6e9d", "idea_id": "leap-02", "library": "sqlparse", "not_applicable": null, "outcome": "idea", "position": 2, "reason": null, "run": 2, "seed": "portfolio-leap-2026-11", "steps_present": "1,2,3", "steps_required": 3, "title": "TokenList.flatten: explicit stack of list iterators instead of recursive 'yield ...", "tool": null}, {"cell": 13, "deal_round": 2, "failure": null, "framework": "skiena", "functions": null, "hypothesis_id": null, "idea_id": null, "library": "sqlparse", "not_applicable": 6, "outcome": "not_applicable", "position": 3, "reason": null, "run": 2, "seed": "portfolio-leap-2026-11", "steps_present": "1,2,3,4,5,6", "steps_required": 6, "title": null, "tool": null}], "repo": "sqlparse", "round": 2, "see